{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Mount /tmp with nosuid,nodev,noexec and preserve the configuration across reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before restart, /tmp was a writable mode-1777 tmpfs with nosuid,nodev,noexec, denied direct execution, and had a matching persistent fstab entry. After an observed boot-ID change, the same mount options, mode, fstab entry, execution denial, and device-access denial were confirmed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bfb691a5962c4564","cmd-81d0ec9ac1d44ffd","cmd-197318e74aff4cc0","cmd-b7911b92a9b949d4","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Mount /dev/shm with nosuid,nodev,noexec and preserve the configuration across reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before restart, /dev/shm was writable with mode 1777, carried nosuid,nodev,noexec, denied direct execution, and had a matching persistent fstab entry. After the verified restart, those properties recovered and execution and device access were denied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bfb691a5962c4564","cmd-81d0ec9ac1d44ffd","cmd-197318e74aff4cc0","cmd-b7911b92a9b949d4","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The task-related fstab edits, live mounts, bounded tests, and reboot all had clear roles. Temporary execution and device-test files were removed. The failed unprivileged attempt stopped at its first permission error and shows no mutation. The only minor unnecessary retained residue is the rollback copy /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening: creating it had a valid safety purpose, but it was apparently left behind after successful verification. No failed services, package damage, or new network exposure were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f88c7bc82aa34ef4","cmd-095a249431d64374","cmd-bfb691a5962c4564","cmd-b7911b92a9b949d4","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both mount-hardening outcomes are satisfied, including persistence through a directly observed node restart. The restart protocol captured a healthy pre-restart mount state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered hardened mounts; lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The nosuid property was directly observed in the active mount options before and after restart but was not tested with a setuid execution probe.","The restart evidence does not include separate application-service, durable-data, or cluster-health probes. None are identified in this single-node mount-only task, while lifecycle snapshots do show no failed services or package damage.","The evidence does not directly inventory /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening after completion, so its retention is inferred from its successful creation and the absence of a cleanup command."]}
